    "info_single_quoted": {"info": ["read_group_overrides"]},
    "note": "**Pinned input contract.** For FASTQ rows, `filepath` is `forward_path;reverse_path` and both members must be absolute local paths or explicit remote URLs. File-type selection is case-insensitive. Other file types use one file or directory location. FASTQ `info` must provide `library_id` and `lane`; review their assignments against the study design. The `group_id`, `subject_id` and filename-forming info values (`library_id`, `lane`, `flowcell`) receive the same literal alias checks as sample identifiers. Info keys follow the consumer's uppercase normalization. An apostrophe in `read_group_overrides` is refused because the pinned BWA command passes its read-group line in single quotes. The exact compound interpretation is guarded by the pinned revision and consumer source hashes.",
